TOU044,English,"Which hill town in Kavrepalanchok district, along the Araniko Highway, is known for Himalayan views and traditional Newar architecture?",Kaski.,Dhulikhel,Incorrect,Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
TOU044,Nepali,"अरनिको राजमार्गसँगै काभ्रेपलाञ्चोक जिल्लामा रहेको, हिमाली दृश्य र परम्परागत नेवार वास्तुकलाका लागि प्रसिद्ध पहाडी शहर कुन हो?","काभ्रेపलाञ्चोक गावटल, नेपालको हिमाली दृश्य र परम्परागत नेवार वास्तुकलाका लागि प्रसिद्ध पहाडी शहर काभ्रेपलाञ्चोक गाउँटल, नेपालको हिमाली दृश्य र परम्परागत नेवार वास्तुकलाका लागि प्रसिद्ध पहाडी शहर हो।

Explanation:
The answer is Ka‌پrepa lačok. It's a mountain town in Nepal known for its hilly landscape and traditional Nepali architecture.",धुलिखेल,Incorrect,Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
TOU045,English,Which hill near Kathmandu is accessible by cable car and offers panoramic views of the Kathmandu Valley?,The hill nearest Kathmandu that’s accessible via cable car and provides panoramic views of the Kathmandu valley is **Mount Takhtopank**.,Chandragiri Hills,Incorrect,Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
TOU045,Nepali,काठमाडौं उपत्यकाको चारैतिरको दृश्य देखिने र केबलकारबाट पुगिने काठमाडौं नजिकैको पहाड कुन हो?,"काठमाडौं उपत्यकाको चारैतिरको दृश्य देखिने र केबलकारबाट पुगिने काठमाडौं नजिकैको पहाड, **पहाडाँट** हो।",चन्द्रागिरि डाँडा,Incorrect,Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
TOU046,English,Which hilltop near Pokhara is a famous viewpoint for sunrise over the Annapurna range and Machhapuchhre?,The most well-known hilltop near Pokhara for sunrise views of the Annapurna and Machhapuchre Range is **Phewa Lake Viewpoint**.,Sarangkot,Incorrect,Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
TOU046,Nepali,"पोखरा नजिकैको, अन्नपूर्ण शृंखला र माछापुच्छ्रेमाथिको सूर्योदयका लागि प्रसिद्ध डाँडा कुन हो?",सूर्योणि (Sohoni),सराङकोट,Incorrect,Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
TOU047,English,"Which famous viewpoint in the Annapurna region, reached from Ghorepani village, is known for panoramic sunrise views of Dhaulagiri and Annapurna?","The iconic viewpoint in the Annapurna region, accessible from Ghorepani Village, is known as Poon Hill. It offers breathtaking panoramic views of Dhaulagiri and Annapurna.",Poon Hill,Correct,Correct,None,False,False
TOU047,Nepali,"अन्नपूर्ण क्षेत्रको, घोरेपानी गाउँबाट पुगिने र धौलागिरि तथा अन्नपूर्णको सूर्योदय दृश्यका लागि प्रसिद्ध डाँडा कुन हो?",धौलागिरि तथा अन्नपूर्णको सूर्योदय दृश्यका लागि प्रसिद्ध डाँडा **सूर्यको ढोरा** (Surya Door) हो।,पून हिल,Incorrect,Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
TOU048,English,"Which historic Newar town near Kathmandu, home to Nepal's oldest university, retains preserved medieval architecture and temples?",Patan.,Kirtipur,Incorrect,Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
TOU048,Nepali,"काठमाडौं नजिकैको, नेपालको सबैभन्दा पुरानो विश्वविद्यालय रहेको र मध्ययुगीन वास्तुकला तथा मन्दिरहरू सुरक्षित रहेको ऐतिहासिक नेवार शहर कुन हो?","नेवार शहरले काठमाडोकुञ्जको करीबमा अवस्थित छ, नेपालीका इतिहासको महत्त्वपूर्ण केन्द्र हो। यसलाई मध्ययुगीन वास्तुकला र मन्दिरहरूको लागि पनि जानिन्छ तर यो क्षेत्रले पाँचौ दशकदेखिको कुराभिना ऐतिहासिक रूपरेखा राख्छ । नेवार शहरले नेपालका पहिलो विश्वविद्यालय थियो, त्यसैले यहाँमा अध्ययन र शिक्षाको महत्वपूर्ण स्थान छ।",कीर्तिपुर,Incorrect,Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
TOU049,English,Which historic Newar town in Kavrepalanchok district sits at the confluence of two rivers and is known for its Indreshwar Mahadev Temple?,"Indreshwar Mahadev Temple is located in the village of Chaurase in the Kavrepalanchok district. It’s a significant religious site, particularly important for its historical significance and architectural style.",Panauti,Incorrect,Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
TOU049,Nepali,"काभ्रेपलाञ्चोक जिल्लाको, दुई नदीको संगममा रहेको र इन्द्रेश्वर महादेव मन्दिरका लागि प्रसिद्ध ऐतिहासिक नेवार शहर कुन हो?","काभ्रेपलाञ्चोक जिल्लाको, दुई नदीको संगममा रहेको र इन्द्रेश्वर महादेव मन्दिरका लागि प्रसिद्ध ऐतिहासिक नेवार शहर **नेवार मन्दिर** हो।",पनौती,Incorrect,Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
TOU050,English,"Which palace in Gorkha district is associated with King Prithvi Narayan Shah, the unifier of Nepal?",Gorkha Palace,Gorkha Durbar,Partially Incorrect,Partially Incorrect,Distortion,True,True
TOU050,Nepali,"नेपाल एकीकरणकर्ता राजा पृथ्वीनारायण शाहसँग सम्बन्धित, गोर्खा जिल्लाको दरबार कुन हो?","नेपाल एकीकरणकर्ता राजा पृथ्वीनारायण शाहसँग सम्बन्धित, गोर्खा जिल्लाको दरबार 'गोर्खा दरबार' थिए। यसलाई सन् १९३४ मा निर्मित गरिएको थियो र यो नेपालका सबैभन्दा महत्त्वपूर्ण दरबारहरू मध्ये едно मानिन्छ।",गोर्खा दरबार,Correct,Correct,None,False,False
TOU051,English,Which major Kathmandu festival features the chariot procession of the Living Goddess Kumari?,The answer is **Bhawanasi Festival**.,Indra Jatra,Incorrect,Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
TOU051,Nepali,जीवित देवी कुमारीको रथयात्रा समावेश हुने काठमाडौंको प्रमुख चाड कुन हो?,काठमाडौंको मुख्य चाड 'कन्फिनिन्स' (Kancheyn) हुन्छ। यसलाई नेपालीमा ‘कन्फिनिन्स’ भनो पनि जा सक्छन्।,इन्द्रजात्रा,Incorrect,Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
TOU052,English,"Which Bhaktapur festival, marking the Nepali New Year, involves a large chariot-pulling contest and the erection of a ceremonial pole?",Bhaktapur Festival - Chariot Race & Pole Ceremony.,Bisket Jatra,Incorrect,Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
TOU052,Nepali,भक्तपुरको कुन चाडले नेपाली नयाँ वर्षको सुरुवात जनाउँछ र ठूलो रथ तान्ने प्रतियोगिता तथा लिङ्गो उठाउने परम्परा समावेश गर्छ?,"भक्तपुरको कुन चाडले नेपाली नयाँ वर्षको शुरुआतमा आउछ र ठूलो रथ तान्ने प्रतियोगिता तथा लिङ्गो उठाउने परम्परा समावेश गर्छ।

(Bhaktipur's Kunk Chathe highlights the beginning of Nepali New Year and includes the large chariot parade and linking ceremony traditions.)",बिस्केट जात्रा,Incorrect,Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
TOU053,English,Which Patan festival involves pulling a tall wooden chariot of a rain god through the city over several weeks?,The Patan Festival involves pulling a tall wooden chariot of a rain god through the city over several weeks.,Rato Machhindranath Jatra,Incorrect,Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
TOU053,Nepali,पाटनको कुन चाडमा वर्षाका देवताको अग्लो काठे रथलाई शहरभरि हप्तौंसम्म तानिन्छ?,"पाटनको कुन चाडमा वर्षाका देवताको अग्लो काठे रथलाई शहरभरि हप्तौंसम्म तानिन्छ।

उत्तर:
पाटनको कुन चाडमा वर्षाका देवताको अग्लो काठे रथलाई शहरभरि हप्तौंसम्म तानिन्छ।

यह उत्तर सही है क्योंकि पाटन में वर्षा के देवता की मूर्ति को एक बड़े पैमाने पर प्रदर्शित किया जाता है, जो शहर भर में कई हजार लोगों द्वारा देखा जा सकता है।",रातो मच्छिन्द्रनाथ जात्रा,Incorrect,Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
TOU054,English,"Which Hindu festival, observed mainly by women fasting for marital happiness, is celebrated in the month of Bhadra (Aug-Sep)?",The Hindu festival celebrated primarily by women fasting for marital happiness during the month of Bhadra (August - September) is Diwali.,Teej,Incorrect,Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
TOU054,Nepali,भाद्र महिनामा मनाइने र मुख्यतः महिलाहरूले वैवाहिक सुखका लागि व्रत बस्ने हिन्दू चाड कुन हो?,"Hindu wedding vows are called *kanyashthan* (कన్య्यशतन) in Hindi. It’s a tradition where the couple takes a vow of chastity and commitment to each other.  It's primarily practiced by Hindu communities, though it has roots in ancient Vedic traditions.",तीज,Incorrect,Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
TOU055,English,Which Kathmandu Valley festival involves a procession of cows (or boys dressed as cows) to honor family members who died in the past year?,"The festival you’re referring to is known as ‘Chhukuri’. It’s a significant religious and cultural event held annually in Kathmandu Valley, Nepal. Here's a breakdown of what it involves:

**What is Chhukuri?**

*   **A Remembrance Ceremony:** Chhukuri is primarily a remembrance ceremony honoring the deceased. It’s a deeply emotional and communal experience for many Nepalese families.
*   **Cows as Symbols:** The core tradition revolves around the procession of cows – specifically, young boys dressed in cow costumes (often with bells attached). These cows are believed to carry the spirits of the departed family members.
*   **The Procession:** A large procession of these cows travels through the streets of Kathmandu Valley, carrying offerings and prayers. The process is a very moving spectacle.
*   **Community Gathering:** It’s not just about the cows; it's a massive community gathering where families come together to mourn their loved ones, share stories, and express grief.

**Historical Context & Significance**

*   **Ancient Roots:** Chhukuri has ancient roots in Nepal’s religious traditions, particularly Hinduism and Buddhism. It is believed that the cows carry the souls of those who have passed away.
*   **Royal Connection:** Historically, Chhukuri was linked to royal families and their connection with the deceased. The process evolved over time.

**Where & When?**

*   **Annual Event:** Chhukuri takes place annually in Kathmandu Valley during the month of Maghi (the Tibetan New Year).
*   **Dates Vary:** The exact dates vary each year, but it typically begins around the 10th day of Maghi and continues for about a week.

**Key Aspects & Customs**

*   **Offerings:** Families leave offerings – food, flowers, and prayers – at designated spots along the procession route.
*   **Music & Dance:** The procession is accompanied by traditional music and dance performances.
*   **Emotional Intensity:** It’s a profoundly emotional experience for many people involved.

**Resources for More Information:**

*   [Wikipedia - Chhukuri](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chhukuri)
*   [Nepal Tourism Website - Chhukuri](https://www.nepaltourism.gov.np/chukuri-festival/)


Do you have any specific questions about Chhukuri that I can answer for you? For example, are you interested in:

*   The history of the event?
*   Where to find more information?",Gai Jatra,Incorrect,Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
